tán relacionados con un mismo proyecto.","en":"What the data shows: Between 2023 and 2025, this body awarded 48 minor contracts for services and supplies above 14,000 and up to 15,000 euros, just under the legal limit. If those amounts were spread as in the band immediately below, 13.6 contracts would be expected. The observed-to-expected ratio is 3.5, with a 95% confidence interval of 2.4 to 5.2. December accounts for 19% of the contracts just under the limit, compared with 14% of all its services and supplies contracts. The awardee with the most contracts just under the limit, called awardee A here, has 3. Contract [1], for 14,500 euros, was awarded in December 2025.\nWhat it cannot show: The concentration of contracts in December does not indicate improper behavior. Similar trends could result from seasonal demand or budget constraints. The number of contracts near the limit does not prove violations, as market prices or fixed budgets may influence amounts.\nWhat can be checked: Check the dates and values of contracts [1] and [2] to confirm if they align with the December trend. Review awardee A's contracts to see if multiple contracts serve the same purpose. Verify if contracts [3] were part of a larger procurement plan for the same service.","origen_es":"modelo","origen_en":"modelo","modelo":"Qwen3-4B (Q4_K_M, llama.cpp)","regla":"ss","citas":["3UhzpqRpHnOdkQsA7ROvsg%3D%3D","os%2FfWejKnXQadbH3CysQuQ%3D%3D","wGIYxvvA0aCcCF8sV%2BqtYA%3D%3D"],"generado":"2026-11-16"}}